<title>AUSTRALIA: Woodside, Shell win Timor Sea permits.</title>
<headline>Woodside, Shell win Timor Sea permits.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Oil's Shell Development (Australia) Pty Ltd, Woodside Petroleum Ltd and Cultus Petroleum had bid successfully for petroleum exploration premrits in the Timor Sea, Australian Resources and Energy Minister Warwrick Parer said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Parer said in a statement consortia lead by Indo Pacific Energy Ltd, Coastal Oil and Gas Corp, Hardy Oil &amp; Gas Plc, Cartier Oil Pty Ltd and Nippon Oil Exploration Ltd had also each won one of the nine permits on offer.</p>
<p>&quot;During the next six years, an estimated A$305 million will be spent on exploration in these areas,&quot; Parer said.</p>
<p>&quot;This will include at 24 exploration wells,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
